# Old Mill Road, seed 7, hand play by Code (systems entry)
# turn 1: let the brigand come
end
# turn 2: the captain kills it alone, two certain hits
move captain 3,7
attack captain brigand-1
move wren 2,7
wait wren
end
# turn 3: toward the fort, outside the wake radius
move wren 4,5
wait wren
move captain 4,6
wait captain
end
# turn 4: Wren to the road below the fort, still outside radius 4
move wren 6,3
wait wren
move captain 4,3
wait captain
end
# turn 5: Wren takes the fort and wakes the mill; the captain stays out of the bow line
move wren 6,2
wait wren
wait captain
end
# turn 6: Wren finishes the soldier from the fort; the captain opens on the archer, which cannot answer at one tile
attack wren soldier-1
move captain 7,2
attack captain archer-1
end
# turn 7: the captain climbs the hill and finishes the archer
move captain 8,2
attack captain archer-1
wait wren
end
# turn 8: the captain, at 7 after the archer, takes the fort; Wren stages on the road out of the bandit's reach
move wren 8,3
wait wren
move captain 6,2
wait captain
end
# turn 9: the fort's heal plus the dressing, since the mill bandit's two swings are 18 and the captain must open with more than that
item captain 2
wait wren
end
# turn 10: one more fort heal on the phase start, then stage at the road under the boss, who never moves
move captain 9,3
wait captain
wait wren
end
# turn 11: the captain opens alone and takes the counter and the enemy-phase swing; Wren stays out of reach, because the bandit's 10 is half her HP
move captain 10,2
attack captain mill_bandit-1
wait wren
end
# turn 12: the last turn of the limit. Wren opens at full HP and it ends before anyone counters
move wren 9,1
attack wren mill_bandit-1
